 "capsule": "Albania declared independence from the Ottoman Empire on 28 November 1912 at Vlorë under Ismail Qemali and won great-power recognition with contracted borders at the 1913 Conference of London, passing through the short reign of Wilhelm of Wied, wartime occupations, and the rise of Ahmet Zogu from prime minister (1922) to president (1925) to King Zog I (1928). Italy invaded and annexed the kingdom in April 1939, and after German occupation collapsed in 1944 the communist-led National Liberation Front took power, proclaiming the People's Republic on 11 January 1946 under Enver Hoxha.",
